  "question": {
    "text": "Given : $\\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{Fe}^{3+} / \\mathrm{Fe}}^{\\circ}=-0.036 \\mathrm{~V}, \\quad \\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+} / \\mathrm{Fe}}^{\\circ}=-0.439 \\mathrm{~V}$. The value of standard electrode potential for the change, $\\mathrm{Fe}_{(\\text {aq })}^{3+}+\\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}(\\mathrm{aq})$ will be :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$-0.072 \\mathrm{~V}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$0.385 \\mathrm{~V}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$0.770 \\mathrm{~V}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-0.270$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\because \\mathrm{Fe}^{3+}+3 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Fe} ; \\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}=-0.036 \\mathrm{~V} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\Delta \\mathrm{G}_1^{\\circ}=-\\mathrm{nFE}^{\\circ}=-3 \\mathrm{~F}(-0.036) \\\\\n& =+0.108 \\mathrm{~F} \\\\\n& \\text { Also } \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}+2 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Fe} ; \\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}=-0.439 \\mathrm{~V} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\Delta \\mathrm{G}_2^{\\circ}=-\\mathrm{nFE}^{\\circ} \\\\\n& =-2 \\mathrm{~F}(-0.439) \\\\\n& =0.878 \\mathrm{~F} \\\\\n& \\text { To find } \\mathrm{E}^{\\circ} \\text { for } \\mathrm{Fe}_{(\\mathrm{aq})}^{3+}+\\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}(\\mathrm{aq}) \\\\\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}=-\\mathrm{nFE}{ }^{\\circ}=-1 \\mathrm{FE} \\circ \\\\\n& \\because \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}=\\mathrm{G}_1^{\\circ}-\\mathrm{G}_2^{\\circ} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}=0.108 \\mathrm{~F}-0.878 \\mathrm{~F} \\\\\n& \\therefore-\\mathrm{FE}^{\\circ}=+0.108 \\mathrm{~F}-0.878 \\mathrm{~F} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}=0.878-0.108 \\\\\n& =0.77 \\mathrm{~V}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}